-- title:
--   Places containing j detect the j-chart up to varpi-powers
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring (a domain with the `IsDiscreteValuationRing` structure) and let $\varpi \in R$ be such that the maximal ideal of $R$ is the principal ideal $(\varpi)$. Let $K_0$ be a field which is an $R$-algebra and a fraction field of $R$, and let $F$ be a field which is an algebra over both $R$ and $K_0$, compatibly (scalar tower). Let $j \in F$ be nonzero, and assume $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K_0(j)$ obtained by adjoining $j$ to $K_0$ inside $F$. Let $x \in F$ be such that for every place $v$ of $F$ over $K_0$ — that is, every valuation subring of $F$ which contains the image of $K_0$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring — with $j$ in its valuation subring, also $x$ lies in that valuation subring. The conclusion is that there exists $k \in \mathbb{N}$ with $(\varpi)^k x \in$ `chartAlgFin R F j`, where $\varpi$ is taken in $F$ via the structure map and `chartAlgFin R F j` is the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[j]$ generated by $j$, i.e. the integral closure of $R[j]$ in $F$.
--
--   This is the local-global dictionary for the finite chart of the two-chart integral model: up to bounded powers of the uniformiser, the affine chart ring is cut out inside $F$ by the places at which $j$ is regular. It is used in [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_divisor_degree_pos_lSpaceOn_nsmul_le_of_branchData`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_divisor_degree_pos_lSpaceOn_nsmul_le_of_branchData), applied both to $j$ and to its inverse to cover the two charts.
